---
onetaskgraph_template: 1
description: A concise preview of the measurements a draft's actual spike agents will make.
variables:
  overview:
    description: >-
      Nonempty prose stating the phase, what is being measured and why. Use a few lines;
      at most 250 whitespace-separated words. No placeholder answers.
    type: string
    required: true
  spikes:
    description: >-
      One object for each actual spike-agent ID, with nonempty string fields spike,
      question and use. State the question measured and how its answer will be used,
      in one or two lines per agent. Each rendered headed section, including its heading,
      has its own 250-whitespace-word cap. No grouped, missing or duplicate agents.
    type: list
    items: object
    required: true
---
{% block brief_guidance %}
{# Overview first, then one identified question/use section per actual spike agent.
   Answer from the local draft and spike tasks. Omit architecture, budgets, scheduling
   and design approval. All fields contain substantive answers rather than placeholders.
   Overview and each headed section have independent caps; there is no total word cap. #}
{% endblock %}
{% block overview %}
{{ overview }}
{% endblock %}
{% block spikes %}
{% for item in spikes %}
## {{ item.spike }}

Question: {{ item.question }}

Use: {{ item.use }}

{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
